      "form_guide": "",
      "comment": "Grand pacer SWAYZEE (4) was brave in his resuming effort, coming from the back row and working to the front before sticking on for a 1.3m fourth in the Geelong Cup. Prefer him over further than the mile but his second-up record is strong so he should be improved. Aided by a good draw and if anywhere near his best he'll be too good for these. ITS CONFIDENTIAL (9) made a winning start for Brad Hewitt at his latest appearance, beating some handy rivals when scoring by 2 metres at Bathurst. Draws wide but he strikes at 50 per cent here. HEZA PUNK ROCKER NZ (8) was good in his first outing for Seaton Grima last week, coming from a similar draw to place at Listed level at this circuit and distance. Expect him to feature in the finish again. RIPP (10) has exotic claims off a win from a similar barrier here two back.",
